### Notes (why no scores)

- Exo Free was a stealth slot: OpenCode's own docs describe it only as "available on OpenCode for a limited time. The team is using this time to collect feedback and improve the model." No vendor, no model card, no weights.
- It was added to the Zen docs (commit `e2564336`, PR #53622) with the 1M/131K specs and removed within days; the id now returns HTTP 410 ModelDeprecated.
- No benchmark tracker (Artificial Analysis, BenchLM, BenchmarkList, Vals) carries measured scores for `exo-free`; only registry rows (Sulat) and a YouTube short exist, with no evaluation.
- Because the vendor was never identified, no proxy model can be substituted and no verified numbers exist. Treat as unmeasured.

No normalized 1–100 scores are assigned.

